  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{1,3,5,\u2026,49},{51,53,55,\u2026,99}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{1,3,5,\u2026,99},{2,4,6,\u2026,98}}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $2$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- ${{1,3,5,\u2026,49},{41,43,45,\u2026,99}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{1,3,5,\u2026,69},{70,71,72,\u2026,99}}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $70$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- ${{1,3,5,\u2026,39},{51,53,55,\u2026,99}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) do not appear in any subsets.",
